## Security Monitoring

Both DC01 and W11-Attack are enrolled as Wazuh agents.

```text
+----------------+                    +----------------+
|      DC01      |                    |   W11-Attack   |
|                |                    |                |
| Windows Logs   |                    | Windows Logs   |
| Sysmon         |                    | Sysmon         |
+-------+--------+                    +-------+--------+
        |                                     |
        |          Wazuh Agent                |
        +------------------+------------------+
                           |
                           v
                    +-------------+
                    |    Wazuh    |
                    |  SIEM / XDR |
                    | 10.20.0.60  |
                    +-------------+
```

Sysmon is installed on both Windows systems and provides additional endpoint telemetry beyond the standard Windows event logs.

Wazuh collects the Sysmon operational event channel:

```text
Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational
```

This allows endpoint activity to be correlated with Wazuh detection rules.

---

## Telemetry Validation

Logging was validated by executing administrative and enumeration commands on the monitored Windows systems.

Example commands include:

```powershell
whoami
net user
net group "Domain Admins" /domain
Get-ADUser -Filter *
```

The resulting process activity was recorded by Sysmon and successfully forwarded through the Wazuh agent to the Wazuh server.

This validates the telemetry pipeline:

```text
User / System Activity
        |
        v
Windows + Sysmon
        |
        v
Wazuh Agent
        |
        v
Wazuh Manager
        |
        v
Detection Rules
        |
        v
Wazuh Dashboard
```

Wazuh alerts, including high-severity alerts, have been successfully generated from endpoint activity.

